\par Report the Fall 200}{\cf1\insrsid6750727 5}{\cf1\insrsid9600684 
 ratio of full-time equivalent students (full-time plus 1/3 part time) to full-time equivalent instructional faculty (full time plus 1/3 part time). In the ratio calculations, exclude both faculty and stud
ents in stand-alone graduate or professional programs such as medicine, law, veterinary, dentistry, social work, business, or public health in which faculty teach virtually only graduate level students. Do not count undergraduate or graduate student teach
ing assistants as faculty.
\par 
\par Fall 200}{\cf1\insrsid6750727 5}{\cf1\insrsid9600684  Student to Fac}{\cf1\insrsid3308450 ulty ratio:  }{\ul\cf1\insrsid13260534\charrsid13260534 14.1}{\cf1\insrsid3308450  to }{\cf1\insrsid3308450\charrsid6750727 1 (based on }{
\ul\cf1\insrsid13260534\charrsid13260534 10,349}{\cf1\insrsid3308450\charrsid6750727  students and }{\ul\cf1\insrsid13260534\charrsid13260534 736}{\cf1\insrsid3308450\charrsid6750727  faculty).}{\cf1\insrsid9600684 
\par \page }{\b\cf1\insrsid9600684 I-3. Undergraduate Class Size
\par }{\cf1\insrsid9600684 
\par In the table below, please use the following definitions to report information about the size of classes and class sections offered in the Fall 200}{\cf1\insrsid6750727 5}{\cf1\insrsid9600684  term.
\par 
\par }{\b\i\cf1\insrsid9600684 Class Sections:}{\cf1\insrsid9600684 
  A class section is an organized course offered for credit, identified by discipline and number, meeting at a stated time or times in a classroom or similar setting, and not a subsection such as a laboratory or discussion session. Undergraduate class sec
tions are defined as any sections in which at least one degree-seeking undergraduate student is enrolled for credit. Exclude}{\b\cf1\insrsid9600684  }{\cf1\insrsid9600684 
distance learning classes and noncredit classes and individual instruction such as dissertation or thesis research, music instructio
n, or one-to-one readings. Exclude students in independent study, co-operative programs, internships, foreign language taped tutor sessions, practicums, and all students in one-on-one classes. Each class section should be counted only once and should not 
be duplicated because of course catalog cross-listings.
\par 
\par }{\b\i\cf1\insrsid9600684 Class Subsections:}{\cf1\insrsid9600684   A class subsection includes any subsection of a course, such as laboratory, recitation, and discussion subsections that are supplementary in nature and are scheduled to meet separa
tely from the lecture portion of the course. Undergraduate subsections are defined as any subsections of courses in which degree-seeking undergraduate students enrolled for credit. As above, exclude noncredit classes and individual instruction such as dis
sertation or thesis research, music instruction, or one-to-one readings. Each class subsection should be counted only once and should not be duplicated because of cross-listings.
\par 
\par Using the above definitions, please report for each of the following class-size intervals the number of }{\i\cf1\insrsid9600684 class sections}{\cf1\insrsid9600684  and }{\i\cf1\insrsid9600684 class subsections}{\cf1\insrsid9600684  offered in Fall 200}{
\cf1\insrsid7883500 5}{\cf1\insrsid9600684 . For example, a lecture class with 800 students who met at another time in 40 separate labs with 20 students should be counted once in the \'93100+\'94 column in the class section column and 40 times under the 
\'9320-29\'94 column of the class subsections table. 
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s1\qc \li0\ri702\keepn\widctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\adjustright\rin702\lin0\itap0 \b\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cf1\insrsid9600684 Number of Class Sections with Undergraduates Enrolled
